# ChatADHD — the first wall in front of loom-server for use without an account (R103 B2). For package B3 to apply.
#
# Every number here is a PRESET (owner rule: nothing is a fixed cap); raise or remove any of them. None of them
# replaces the limits inside loom-server (server_accounts.pack -> guests.protection): only the server knows which
# session and which key a request belongs to. Caddy only stops floods early and cheaply.
#
# How to use (B3):
#   1. In the site block of /etc/caddy/Caddyfile (managed by deploy/install.sh) add:   import /etc/caddy/chatadhd-guests.caddy
#      and copy this file there. The reverse_proxy of the site block stays as it is (it sets X-Forwarded-For to the
#      real client address, overwriting whatever the client sent).
#   2. loom-server MUST then trust that header, or every guest shares the address 127.0.0.1 and the per-address limits
#      hit everybody at once: overlay <accounts_root>/profiles/server_accounts.pack with
#        {"schema":"loom.runtime_profile_overlay/1","domain":"server_accounts","overrides":{"throttle":{"trust_forwarded_for":true}}}
#   3. Part B (guests-ratelimit.caddy, imported the same way) needs Caddy built with the rate-limit module (github.com/mholt/caddy-ratelimit):
#        xcaddy build --with github.com/mholt/caddy-ratelimit      (check: caddy list-modules | grep rate_limit)
#      and, in the global options block at the top of the Caddyfile:   order rate_limit before reverse_proxy
#      Without the module, do not import guests-ratelimit.caddy — part A works with a stock Caddy.
#   4. caddy validate --config /etc/caddy/Caddyfile && systemctl reload caddy

# ── Part A: stock Caddy ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Starting a guest session carries only a challenge and a nonce: a large body there is never legitimate.
@guest_start path /api/auth/guest /api/auth/guest/challenge
request_body @guest_start {
	max_size 4KB
}
